================================================================================
(2) .ufo/waves/round-55/c1/battery/run-battery.py - two mutants that make the two
    branches of leg (iii) REACHABLE, so that a live kill covers them
================================================================================

This is the sharper finding.  At the frozen configuration NEITHER branch of leg
(iii) can fire at all:

  * clause A (ROW_CAP = 64 MiB): the largest executable maps row that any member of
    the frozen b11909 release can produce is 6,766,592 bytes = 6.453 MiB
    (llama-b11909/llama-connect).  The guard can never fire.
  * clause B (past the member's end): for every one of the 51 regular members of
    the frozen release, the page-rounded end of the executable PT_LOAD lies inside
    the member.  The guard can never fire.

Consequently

    grep -l "not read\|extends past the member" .ufo/waves/round-55/c1/battery/*.out

matches NO receipt: the round-55 C1 kill battery exercises neither branch of leg
(iii).  A mutant that DELETED either guard would still print met=True, and the
frozen build measurement (met=True) therefore carries no evidence for leg (iii)
beyond the guards' presence in the source text.  The two mutants below put a tree
file past each guard's threshold and make the branch reachable on the frozen build.

--- a/.ufo/waves/round-55/c1/battery/run-battery.py
+++ b/.ufo/waves/round-55/c1/battery/run-battery.py
