CAVEAT, stated plainly: these two battery mutants are a DESIGN, not a receipt.
They were not run (a battery run takes three live replays and the lane is
READ-ONLY for this seat); they are the smallest change that would give leg (iii)
live coverage.  Note also that both would need the planted file to be a regular
member of the counter's own archive, or code_observe refuses it earlier with
"is not a regular member of the archive" - so a mutant that reaches clause B at
all must first clear that check (e.g. by re-pointing the tree file at an existing
member and mapping it past its end, which is what m-past-member-end does).

================================================================================
(3) the unit harness, as a permanent lane asset
================================================================================

.ufo/waves/round-55/w1/out/J2RowCap/j2-rowcap-unit-harness.py imports the counter by
path with importlib, drives code_observe() with synthetic maps rows and a fake mem
fd, and (with --real-kernel) against a real child's /proc/<pid>/maps and
/proc/<pid>/mem.  It is the only artifact in the round-55 C1 evidence that
exercises either branch of leg (iii): 42/42 harness checks, four mutants that each
break one guard, both exact boundaries, and the frozen-geometry reachability proof.
Suggested disposition: land it under the lane's tools/ as a unit test for the
counter and have run-battery.py invoke it, so the two branches stay covered.
